;; db: bench_bipartite
;; Triangles on a bipartite graph: the output is EMPTY (no odd cycles), yet
;; binary joins still enumerate every 2-path.  Prefix-existence filters
;; CANNOT rescue this case (every node has edges); it demonstrates the gap
;; that only worst-case-optimal joins close -- documented as a known limit.
table (edge int int)
table (tri int int int)

rule (edge A B) (edge B C) (edge A C) --> (tri A B C)
